{% import "_tasks.jinja" as _t with context -%}# Agent Guide for `{{ repo_name }}`

This file is for AI coding agents working in this repository. It states how
to run the checks and where edits belong. The human-facing contribution
guide is [.github/CONTRIBUTING.md](.github/CONTRIBUTING.md).
{% if kaggle %}
> Kaggle competition project: shared helpers live in `src/utils/`
> (`from utils.config import ...`); competition data goes in `src/input/`
> and predictions are written to `src/output/`. Do not commit data,
> predictions, or logs — they are git-ignored.
{% elif oj_code %}
> Code-submission workspace ({{ oj_kind }}): write solutions as single files
> (e.g. `main.py`). Per-problem folders and `test/` sample cases are created
> by the judge CLI at runtime — do not commit downloaded cases.
{% elif oj_ctf %}
> CTF participant workspace: per-problem starters live in
> `challenges/<category>/<problem>/solve.py`. Run one directly
> (`python challenges/pwn/example/solve.py`), then adapt the offset /
> target. Never commit binaries (`vuln`) or flags — they are git-ignored.
{% elif web_api %}
> Web API service: the application lives in the top-level `app/` package
> (no `<pkg>` library). Run it with `uvicorn app.main:app --reload`.
{% if data_science_layout %}
>
> The data-science layer coexists: `src/` holds the analysis pipeline
> (`data/`, `features/`, `models/`, `visualization/`) and `notebooks/` /
> `reports/` the exploration artifacts. Keep heavy analysis out of `app/`;
> routers expose results computed by `src/` code. Do not commit data,
> models or reports — they are git-ignored.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
